1
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,680
YAMU!

2
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,437
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,840
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

5
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,960
No, that hat was empty.

6
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,180
All right, this could work.

7
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,640
It's got to work.

8
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:17,360
You'll beat that, Baker.

9
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:18,837
Your guess was wrong.

10
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,273
Guess wrong again, and it will cost you.

11
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:27,017
There are still three magical
hats left on the field,

12
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:30,280
and one of them holds a
special surprise just for you.

13
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:34,874
If you destroy the hat that hides my
dark magician, you'll win this duel.

14
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:37,687
Choose the empty one,
and it's my turn again.

15
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,677
But I'm betting you'll pick the hat that

16
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,348
conceals the trap card
I just put into play.

17
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:43,540
A trap card?

18
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,980
Now, which hat will it be?

19
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:48,360
You're taking a big gamble, Yugi.

20
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,424
If he guesses right, it's over.

21
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:59,480
Blue-Eyes White Dragon,
attack the middle hat

22
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:08,900
Well, now you've done it
Activated my trap card, that is

23
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:10,960
Spellbinding Circle

24
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:19,177
A Blue-Eyes White Dragon
is normally unstoppable but

25
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:22,660
once drained of its energy
by the spell-binding circle,

26
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:26,058
it's no match for the full
power of my Dark Magician.

27
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:44,219
And that puts an end to
your blue-eyes white dragon.

28
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,140
Way to go, Yugi!

29
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,180
Another one?

30
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:09,857
And that puts an end to your dark magician
There are only three blue-eyes white

31
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:14,720
dragon cards in the world And they're all
in my deck Your grandpa had the fourth,

32
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:20,240
but I ripped it up But how could I possibly
know that if I'm not really Seto Kaiba?

33
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:21,410
You know,

34
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:23,177
I couldn't believe it
when you beat all three

35
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:25,731
of my Blue Eyes White Dragons with Exodia.

36
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:28,700
But now, without that
monster in your deck,

37
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:32,940
there's absolutely no way
you can win your move.

38
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,337
Everyone heard about your duel with Seto.

39
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,596
That's how this loser knows about it.

40
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:41,340
That's not my brother, Yugi. I'm sure.

41
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:52,000
I am now rerouting the data from
Field 146 at the Duelist Kingdom.

42
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:56,580
After that, we'll be able to confirm
if Yugi Moto is dueling there.

43
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,120
I'm sure he is.

44
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,967
Now show me what you've got.

45
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:02,120
Here it comes. We're in.

46
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:04,140
Now downloading duel data.

47
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,540
You were right.

48
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:07,440
Yugi Moto is in this duel.

49
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,337
Can you show it to me on screen?

50
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:10,250
My pleasure.

51
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:15,029
I think the part you'll find most
interesting is the name of Yugi's opponent.

52
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,090
What?

53
00:04:16,173 --> 00:04:17,680
Is this your idea of a joke?

54
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,140
I never joke.

55
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:24,620
Sensors indicate that the opponent
opposite Yugi is registered as Seto Kaiba,

56
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,520
and he's using your deck.

57
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,002
Pegasus must have taken my deck.

58
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,897
The duelists are tied,

59
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:34,980
and the imposter has his second
blue-eyes white dragon on the field.

60
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:37,597
Yugi defeated the first
one using a combination

61
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:40,080
of the dark magician and magical hats.

62
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:44,560
He currently has 500 points
left and no cards in play.

63
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,000
It's his move.

64
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:49,380
But without Exodia, Yugi can't win.

65
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:54,406
He has no other cards left in his deck
that can beat the Blue-Eyes White Dragon,

66
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,040
let alone two of them.

67
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:58,280
Well then, I hope you have a plan.

68
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:00,480
Yes, but we've got to work fast.

69
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:03,597
Yugi will lose on the next attack
from the Blue-Eyes White Dragon,

70
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,857
unless we decrease its power from here.

71
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:06,777
Can we do that?

72
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:07,690
Oh, yeah.

73
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:10,637
Upload a virus into that
monster's holocomputer.

74
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:13,740
That dragon is about
to get sick. Real sick.

75
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:14,840
Standing by.

76
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,977
But shouldn't we first wait
to see Yugi's next move?

77
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,780
We can't afford to risk
Yugi losing the duel.

78
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,190
Upload.

79
00:05:22,273 --> 00:05:23,660
Viral injection underway.

80
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:32,635
I don't have any monsters that can
withstand his blue-eyes white dragon.

81
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,260
This could be it.

82
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,240
This duel is over, Yugi.

83
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:40,860
I'm sure we'll be hearing the fat
lady sing right after your turn.

84
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,377
I still have defense paralysis active,

85
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:46,989
so whatever monster you pick
won't be able to defend itself.

86
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:50,020
I choose the feral imp in attack mode.

87
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,719
I wish Yugi waited a few
more seconds before moving.

88
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:03,397
Isn't there anything you can do to get
that computer virus uploaded faster?

89
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:05,037
We're already halfway there.

90
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,820
This is as fast as it goes.

91
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:10,880
Viral implant now at 60%, but
it doesn't seem to be working.

92
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:14,957
The Blue-Eyes White Dragon is
still showing no signs of weakness.

93
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,160
Something is wrong.

94
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,440
This is almost too easy.

95
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,920
Yugi! Hang on!

96
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,700
Yugi can still win this.

97
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:27,660
Don't forget, he beat
Kaiba last time. Yugi!

98
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:31,240
It's time, Blue-Eyes White Dragon. Attack!

99
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,160
What are you waiting for?

100
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:40,790
Attack!

101
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,980
The virus is taking effect.

102
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:47,051
Blue-eyes-white dragon's attack
power is beginning to drop.

103
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,977
But it's still too strong.

104
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:52,360
It has to get weaker, or
it'll still beat Yugi.

105
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,960
But I don't believe it.

106
00:06:57,260 --> 00:06:58,640
What's going on?

107
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:00,780
My blue-eyes-white dragon!

108
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,360
This is Kimo to Pegasus.

109
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:13,017
I hope you're watching, sir, because
we got a real problem out here.

110
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,540
How did Yugi do that?

111
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:18,160
It wasn't Yugi, it was Seto Kaiba. How?

112
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:22,060
It seems that the real Kaiba
is still very much alive.

113
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:26,120
The blue-eyes white dragon's
attack power is dropping rapidly.

114
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:30,501
The virus implant is successfully
disabling the monster completely.

115
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:34,340
All right, now let's get to
work on dragon number three.

116
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:36,180
Standing by.

117
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:37,919
What's the matter?

118
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:40,257
We've been locked out
by a remote terminal.

119
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:42,046
Looks like we've been hacked.

120
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,680
Ah, it's Pegasus.

121
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,660
Hey, Kaiba. Move in.

122
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,840
On my mark. Let's go.

123
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,700
Go, go, go, go, go!

124
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:10,600
Attack power is holding now at 2,000.

125
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:12,369
But this should've worked.

126
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:16,860
The Blue-Eyed White Dragon
is launching its attack. No!

127
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:24,200
Now, Blue-Eyed White Dragon,
time to obliterate them! Ha! Ha!

128
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:30,330
Yugi!

129
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,230
Kaiba?

130
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,060
Yu-Gi!

131
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:45,790
Kaiba!

132
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,920
It stopped!

133
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:54,400
The dragon!

134
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,280
This can't be!

135
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,240
It's gone.

136
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:07,740
It's a trick.

137
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:13,460
The blue-eyes white dragon is destroyed,
but the virus was not responsible.

138
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:14,920
Then how?

139
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,800
Did Yugi Moto somehow do this?

140
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:18,820
How could he?

141
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:20,040
It is your deck.

142
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,947
It's the heart of the cards.

143
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:23,460
Yugi was right.

144
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:30,050
Why?

145
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,560
Why me?

146
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:33,290
Why?

147
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:35,520
Because Kaiba's still alive.

148
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:36,702
He stopped you.

149
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:38,850
Silence!

150
00:09:38,933 --> 00:09:41,020
I am Kaiba! Enough!

151
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,020
Your charade is over!

152
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,060
My brother is alive!

153
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,500
What's going on?

154
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:48,060
It's like Yugi said.

155
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:52,615
Last time Yugi dueled my brother, he
showed Seto the heart of the cards.

156
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:57,440
This faker may have taken his death, but
the real Seto Kaiba's alive and well.

157
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,550
Imposter!

158
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:04,180
The real Seto Kaiba
destroyed that monster.

159
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:08,106
I know because I sensed him
calling out to me when it happened.

160
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,180
Now, enough of your lies.

161
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,817
We know you're not Kaiba.

162
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,497
It's time for you to show
us who you really are.

163
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:17,580
I told you, I am Kaiba.

164
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:22,360
Or at least I'm part of
him, the darkest part.

165
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:33,460
I can see you don't recognize me, Yuki.

166
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:36,800
I wasn't lying when I
told you I was Seto Kaiba.

167
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:41,357
The evil part of him that you sent to
the Shadow Realm after our last duel.

168
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:43,700
Now I'm back, thanks to Pegasus.

169
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:47,340
You're not a part of my brother anymore.

170
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:49,077
Ew, it's hideous.

171
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:54,680
I always thought that this duel just might
turn ugly, but I never thought that ugly

172
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,900
Sir, he got away

173
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:05,620
Search the grounds, everywhere

174
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:10,860
Hmm, it appears that young Yugi's
nemesis, the real Seto Kaiba,

175
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:15,017
has come to his rescue I must
admit that this little development

176
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:19,720
is one twist that even I did not
foresee I have some bad news, sir.

177
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,253
The real Kaiba has eluded us once again.

178
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:23,210
You were right.

179
00:11:23,293 --> 00:11:25,357
He was using a terminal
in the Kaiba Mansion

180
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:28,137
to access the Industrial
Illusion's mainframe.

181
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:31,457
If I thought he was alive, I
would have beefed up security.

182
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:33,187
That's two escapes, Croquet.

183
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:35,280
Must I lock you away? Again?

184
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:37,660
Get me Kimo on the radio.

185
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:39,630
Hey, Ugly!

186
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:40,600
If I were you,

187
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:42,977
I'd start worrying about
what my big brother's

188
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:45,837
gonna do to you when he
finally catches up to you.

189
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:48,980
Pegasus Takemo, Seto
Kaiba has gotten away.

190
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,597
Don't lose the little one no matter what.

191
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,510
Understood.

192
00:11:52,593 --> 00:11:54,897
I guess I just don't
know what to call you.

193
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:59,020
I was thinking about monster, but
I didn't want to insult the cards.

194
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:01,160
It's your move.

195
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:06,007
You've got a whole deck to go through
and only one blue-eyes white dragon left.

196
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,840
Grappler in defense mode!

197
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:21,380
He's just biding his time until
he draws his last blue eyes.

198
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:23,220
It's my turn.

199
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,277
I'd play this card in defense mode,

200
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:29,297
but he's still got his defense paralysis
card in play, so I can only attack.

201
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:33,677
And with no defense, if he draws the
blue eyes white dragon, I'm finished.

202
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:38,580
I'll set one card face down on the field
and draw the Celtic Guardian as well,

203
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:39,740
in attack mode.

204
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:51,560
Your grappler split

205
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:57,637
Parting is such sweet sorrow
Next up is Mystic Horseman in

206
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:02,000
defense mode And I'll lay one of
my cards face down just like you

207
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:04,860
Face down?

208
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:07,669
Is it a magic card or
is he setting a trap?

209
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:15,300
Again, I'll lay a card face down And I'll
use the mystical elf in attack mode Plus,

210
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:21,160
this Book of Secret Arts will raise its
attack and defense power by 300 points.

211
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,400
My turn is over.

212
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:32,260
Patience, Yugi, for it
will soon be all over.

213
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,560
Yugi has two cards face
down and three monsters.

214
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:40,417
He must be trying to
strengthen the mystical elf

215
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:43,197
somehow to withstand my
mystic horseman's attack.

216
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:48,520
But if I draw the final blue eyes
and destroy any one of his monsters,

217
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,780
that will take his life
points down to zero anyway.

218
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:55,077
I find it hard to believe,

219
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:58,937
but I'm liking the look on that guy's
face even less than I did before.

220
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:01,220
Wipe that smile off his face, Yugi.

221
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,280
Loser, make your move!

222
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:07,240
As you wish.

223
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:12,920
I'll prepare for the
Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

224
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:20,610
Yugi!

225
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,380
Don't worry, Yugi.

226
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:25,267
My brother will help
out just like last time.

227
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:26,830
Dream on.

228
00:14:26,913 --> 00:14:28,760
Your luck's about to run out.

229
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,374
Just see for yourself.

230
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,060
Unlike the last Blue-Eyes,

231
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:37,777
this one's at full power and your brother's
in no position to do a thing about it.

232
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:41,684
Cause we found where his hiding
place is and now he's on the run.

233
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,900
So that means Kaiba is alive?

234
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:46,797
Dimwit, it means don't
expect another miracle.

235
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:48,980
Cause this duel's about to end.

236
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,580
Oh no!

237
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,700
Such a good dragon.

238
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,453
Wouldn't you say, Yugi?

239
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,097
This duel's about to end now.

240
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:04,460
Go, white lightning attack!

241
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:09,080
This duel's not over yet.

242
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,300
Activate mirror force now!

243
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:15,910
Whoa!

244
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:17,846
He's turned over a trap card!

245
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:21,234
The mirror force reflects
your attack right back at you!

246
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:27,560
Pretty good trick, but I'm
ready with one of my own.

247
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,180
I'll use negate attack!

248
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:35,120
Oh, we had a magic card
waiting just in case.

249
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:41,100
Negate attack neutralizes any attack
thrown at me, even if it's one of my own.

250
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,840
Yugi, it's all over.

251
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:51,100
It's time to finish this duel
with Reborn the Monster. Oh, no.

252
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:55,834
That allows you to revive any monster
lost in this duel from either deck.

253
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,557
I'm glad you know the rules.

254
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,460
Now guess which card I want.

255
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,860
Be reborn, Blue Eyes, White Dragon.

256
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:15,940
That lot of good that
move's gonna do you, Yugi.

257
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,940
Both of these monsters are evenly matched.

258
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,120
Their powers are not the same.

259
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:24,597
You forgot about my mystical elf.

260
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:28,033
She's been chanting a spell
since I put her on the field.

261
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:31,377
It allows the mystical elf to transfer her

262
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:34,560
own attack power to any
other monster I choose.

263
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:36,530
What?

264
00:16:36,613 --> 00:16:37,443
This can't be!

265
00:16:37,526 --> 00:16:39,980
This move was inspired
by Seto Kaiba himself.

266
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:44,737
He showed me that you can alter the
attack power of a blue-eyes white dragon.

267
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:49,780
But I'm raising the power of mine instead
of lowering it like Kaiba did to yours.

268
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:53,737
This can't be happening! Oh no! No!

269
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:57,140
Consider this a message
from the real Seto Kaiba.

270
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:58,560
You lose!

271
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,440
Now, blue eyes, obliterate!

272
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,897
Pegasus may have helped you escape
the Shadow Realm once before,

273
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:23,509
but it won't happen again.

274
00:17:23,820 --> 00:17:24,920
Never again!

275
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:32,120
Pegasus, I sense that you're watching.

276
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,852
Consider this a warning.

277
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,397
Nothing you send against me will stop me.

278
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:40,120
And when we finally duel,
believe me, victory will be mine.

279
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:42,597
I'll win back my grandfather's soul,

280
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,777
and you will pay for all the people you've

281
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:47,331
hurt in the name of your sick little game.

282
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,920
I'm coming for you, Pegasus.

283
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:59,220
Yugi, you've developed your shadow
powers quite a bit in such a short time.

284
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:05,140
But when we finally duel, believe me,
your Millennium Puzzle will be mine.

285
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,630
Kaiba.

286
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:20,797
That ghost is toast, huh, Yugi?

287
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:24,900
Hey, I knew that the real Kaiba
was alive the whole time. Huh?

288
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:26,890
Hmm?

289
00:18:26,973 --> 00:18:27,803
What is it?

290
00:18:27,886 --> 00:18:29,260
That creep took Mokuba.

291
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:32,140
Huh? Mokuba!

292
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,100
I can't believe it. Mokuba?

293
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,640
He's gone. Taken again.

294
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:37,820
Oh, no.

295
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,980
Hey, Mokuba! Mokuba!

296
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,660
Oh, my God.

297
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:12,120
Oh, my God!
